In California you can no longer buy certain classes of "assault
weapons." Ownership is restricted to original owners, who must
register them. 

> 2.  You must wait 15 days between gun purchase and pick-up.  You must
>     register the gun (Fed and state) at point of purchase.

Technically, what is done is *not* gun registration, though for all
intents and purposes the effect is the same. They call it a
"background check," but of course the results are kept on file and can
be checked by law enforcement.

> 5.  To purchse a weapon (possibly just pistol), you must show proof of
